  "highlights": [
    {
      "title": "Overview",
      "value": "<p>Fresenius University of Applied Sciences (Hochschule Fresenius) is a private, state-recognised German university of applied sciences with a strong international focus. You need not worry about communication, since English-language programmes are available, both at the bachelor’s and master’s levels.</p>",
      "image": null,
      "highlightType": "General"
    },
    {
      "title": "Student life",
      "value": "<p>With over 1,000 international students and multiple campuses, you’ll find peers from diverse backgrounds and dedicated international support. You’ll have a good mix of academics, practical experience, and a supportive, socially active community.</p>",
      "image": null,
      "highlightType": "General"
    },
    {
      "title": "Accommodation",
      "value": "<p>Fresenius University of Applied Sciences does not provide its own student housing/dormitories. However, the International Office helps you in your accommodation search.</p>",
      "image": null,
      "highlightType": "General"
    },
    {
      "title": "Facilities",
      "value": "<p><strong>Library</strong><br>Fresenius has a dedicated library system across its campuses, with both physical and online resources.</p><p><strong>Laboratory</strong><br>At Fresenius, you’ll find many labs related to its science, health, and design programmes. The university also has a research institute called the Institute For Analytical Research (IFAR), focused on analytical chemistry, environmental analytics, and related fields.</p><p><strong>Cafeteria</strong><br>On campus, you’ll find cafeteria-style facilities for snacks, salads, and drinks.</p>",
      "image": null,
      "highlightType": "General"
    }
  ],
